 "description": "This document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html)\nfor Bank Data Sharing APIs for Ozone Connect.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by an financial institution so that Ozone\ncan expose these end-points to TPPs.\n\n#### Implementer Notes\n\nImplementers should note that this API prescribes a positive response for correctly executed\noperations including those where no data is returned. This is consistent with the general principles\nof REST.\nFor example, if the operation \n`get /accounts/{accountId}/products` is invoked and no product data is found for the account\nassociated with the value of `accountId` then the correct response is to return a `200` and an empty\narray: `{ \"data\": [] }`.\n\nPlease refer to the API Hub documentation for details of test cases that are \navailable for this API using the Ozone Connect test suite.\n\n### Versioning\n\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where:\n\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n**Please adhere to the deprecated flags in your implementation. Do not implement deprecated properties when** **implementing new functionality.**\n\n**Please use the OpenAPI description document attached to the page if you reading this in Confluence** **to check for deprecated properties.**\n### v2.1.11\n\n* Removed CAAP-specific headers (`o3-is-caap-consent-operation`, `o3-caap-consent-use-case`), the `availableBalance`\n property on `CbuaeAccount`, and related CAAP-conditional language. CAAP variants of these endpoints have been\n moved to the CAAP Operations OpenAPI description. `accountIds` is now unconditionally required on `get /accounts`.\n\n\n### v2.1.10\n\n* Scoped `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` description to products linked to the account in the path parameter (previously implied all products at the financial institution).\n\n### v2.1.9\n\n* Added `meta` property to `get /accounts/{accountId}/statements` operation.\n\n### v2.1.8\n\n* Changed `floor` to include missing `string` type.\n\n### v2.1.7\n\n* Corrected `localTimeZone` to match required format for standards\n\n### v2.1.6\n\n* Added `availableBalance` property to `get /accounts/{accountId}` for CAAP operations.\n\n* Removed changelog before v2.1.4 to reduce bloat of OpenAPI description.\n\n### v2.1.5\n\n* Added JWE Schema Object to `FinanceRates` as alternative to JSON object response.\n\n* Changed `components` in `CbuaeBalance` from object to array of objects, in line with standards.\n\n### v2.1.4\n\n* Changed `paymentModes` to optional.\n",
